This week: a large provider asked millions of people to reset your password after a breach. We explain what a password reset is for, why a sign-in link beats a reused password, and why you should confirm your email only on the site you signed up to.

Your security code should never travel by mail: banks send theirs by text message, and a good site lets you choose a passkey instead.

Also in this issue: three tools to forget fewer passwords, and a reader's question on two-factor sign-in.

